# Flutter UI: Custom Widgets Only

Mandatory for every generated Flutter UI in this project.

## Custom widgets only

Build UI with `StatelessWidget` or `StatefulWidget` subclasses (or `HookWidget` if the project uses hooks). Do not use Widget-returning functions or methods.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
Widget _buildHeader() {
  return Text(title);
}

Widget buildCard(Animal animal) {
  return ListTile(title: Text(animal.name));
}
```

```dart
// ✅ GOOD
class AnimalHeader extends StatelessWidget {
  const AnimalHeader({super.key, required this.title});
  final String title;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Text(title);
}
```

## One widget per file

Put each custom widget in its own file under a nearby `widgets/` folder (e.g. `lib/features/<feature>/ui/widgets/`).

```dart
// ❌ BAD — multiple widgets or private helpers in the screen file
class AnimalListPage extends StatelessWidget { ... }
class _AnimalTile extends StatelessWidget { ... }
```

```dart
// ✅ GOOD
// lib/features/animals/ui/animal_list_page.dart → AnimalListPage only
// lib/features/animals/ui/widgets/animal_tile.dart → AnimalTile only
```

## Compose screens from widgets

Screens/pages only assemble imported widgets. Do not define large private widget classes or build helpers inline in the screen file.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
class AnimalListPage extends StatelessWidget {
  Widget _buildList(List<Animal> animals) { ... }
}
```

```dart
// ✅ GOOD
class AnimalListPage extends StatelessWidget {
  const AnimalListPage({super.key, required this.controller});
  final AnimalListController controller;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Column(
      children: [
        const AnimalHeader(title: 'Animals'),
        AnimalList(animals: controller.animals),
      ],
    );
  }
}
```

Exception: Widget-returning helpers only when the user explicitly requests that pattern.
